-- title:
--   Cardinality of ℤᵥ/nℤᵥ equals ℓ^{v_ℓ(n)}
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, that is, a nonzero prime ideal $v.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $\mathcal{O}_v =$ `v.adicCompletionIntegers ℚ` denote the valuation ring of the $v$-adic completion of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $\ell$ be a prime natural number whose image in $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $v.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, so that $v$ is the place above $\ell$, and let $n$ be a nonzero natural number. The assertion is that the quotient of $\mathcal{O}_v$ by the principal ideal generated by the image of $n$ in $\mathcal{O}_v$ is finite of cardinality $\ell^{\,e}$, where $e =$ `n.factorization ℓ` is the exponent of $\ell$ in the prime factorisation of $n$; the cardinality is measured by `Nat.card`, which would return $0$ for an infinite quotient, so finiteness is part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the standard local index computation $\#(\mathbb{Z}_\ell/n\mathbb{Z}_\ell) = \ell^{v_\ell(n)}$, stated for the completion of $\mathbb{Q}$ at the place above $\ell$. It serves as the local input for counting indices of lattices and of stabiliser subgroups: it is used in the computations of relative indices of conjugated diagonal subgroups of matrix groups and in the counting of cosets for local boxes attached to Eichler orders in quaternion algebras.
-- source:
